
## Objective

Build and tune custom Wazuh detection rules for two distinct attack categories:

1. **SSH brute-force login attempts** — host-based detection using authentication logs.
2. **Reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)** against DVWA — web-based detection using Apache access logs.

The objective was not simply to make a rule fire, but to ensure that the rule detects the intended **behavior**, minimizes false positives, and maps correctly to the relevant **MITRE ATT&CK technique**.

---

## Lab Environment

| Machine  | OS               | Purpose                             |
| -------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| Ubuntu 1 | Ubuntu 24.04 LTS | Wazuh Manager / custom rules        |
| Ubuntu 2 | Ubuntu 24.04 LTS | Wazuh Agent + DVWA / attack surface |

Custom Wazuh rules were maintained on Ubuntu 1 in:

```text
/var/ossec/etc/rules/local_rules.xml
```

Ubuntu 2 generated the authentication and web activity that was collected by the Wazuh agent and forwarded to the manager.

