# MITRE ATT&CK Mapping

| Detection       | Wazuh Rule | MITRE Technique      | Technique                      |
| --------------- | ---------: | -------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| SSH brute force |   `100020` | `T1110.001`          | Password Guessing              |
| Reflected XSS   |   `100012` | Web attack detection | XSS / Web exploitation context |

For the SSH detection, `T1110.001` directly represents the credential-guessing behavior being detected.

For the XSS detection, the custom rule currently inherits the detection behavior of Wazuh's web-attack rule. The MITRE mapping should therefore be kept consistent with what the underlying rule actually detects rather than assigning a technique solely because the application being tested is DVWA.

